# Physical Glare in Post Processing's tonemap chain on D3D11 (0) or the render graph (1): Whiterun at 13:00 in clear
# weather (sky and sun bright), then Dragonsreach (torches, windows), a shot of each.
# Sub-effects the main session sets in SettingsUser.json, under "PostProcessing":
#   "Physical Glare": { "enabled": true }   (Composite turns itself on with it; Composite must be ported for the graph run)
#   "Depth of Field", "Local Exposure", "Histogram Auto Exposure", "COD Bloom", "Lens Flare", "Motion Blur", "Camera":
#   { "enabled": false }, unless their ORG ports are in the build too.
# Default glare settings are Lens mode (static PSF, made once). For the animated PSF also run with
#   "Physical Glare": { "settings": { "ApertureMode": 1, "TearFilmStrength": 0.78 } }   (the PSF is remade every frame)
# Expect with 1: "[ORG] Post Processing: chain built (input, physical-glare, composite, ..." and "the chain runs on the
# render graph"; the shots match the 0 run. Black or missing glare means the PSF was never made.
# Effects11 must not own the tonemap (its effect off), or Post Processing does not run at all.
CS_ORG_POST_PROCESSING=0
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=600:set timescale to 0;601:set gamehour to 13;602:fw 81a;700:coc Whiterun;2000:fw 81a;2400:dclf:shot=whiterun;2500:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;3600:dclf:shot=dragonsreach
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=3700
